      "title": "Example 4.51",
      "position": 3,
      "nearest_heading": "Power Rule for Integrals",
      "prompt_text": "Verifying an Indefinite Integral Each of the following statements is of the form $\\int f (x) d x = F (x) + C .$ Verify that each statement is correct by showing that $F^{'} (x) = f (x) .$ $\\int \\left(\\right. x + e^{x} \\left.\\right) d x = \\frac{x^{2}}{2} + e^{x} + C$ $\\int x e^{x} d x = x e^{x} - e^{x} + C$",
      "prompt_latex_bits": [
        "\\int f (x) d x = F (x) + C .",
        "F^{'} (x) = f (x) .",
        "\\int \\left(\\right. x + e^{x} \\left.\\right) d x = \\frac{x^{2}}{2} + e^{x} + C",
        "\\int x e^{x} d x = x e^{x} - e^{x} + C"
      ],
      "has_solution": true,
      "source_anchor": "fs-id1165043393824",
      "notes": ""
    },
    {
